WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.589
"Hey, give it back!"
"Why?"

00:00:18.589 --> 00:00:19.789
"You don't need any more!"

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:23.210
"You're a disgusting, fat pig!"
"Mom! Jeff called me a 

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.910
disgusting, fat pig!"

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.359
"Jeff! Do not call your sister a fat pig."

00:00:28.359 --> 00:00:35.359
"Well, she is turning into a little a little porker."
"See? Even dad thinks you're a fat pig."

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:42.420
I was teased a lot because
I'm overweight. 

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.790
A lot of it was behind my back, but then

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:49.710
a lot of it was also to my face.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:53.040
Which, made me feel terrible.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.040
"Hi." 
"Hi."

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.860
"Wouldn't it be quicker if you just smeared that on
your thighs?" /laughter/ "Yeah, can you say 'carbs'?"

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.760
"Meg, you're blocking the sun."

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.650
"Wait, you got a little chocolate right there." /laughter/

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:12.650
I know i'm not the only one. This sort
of thing happens all the time.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.080
My name is Emme, and as the first plus-sized
supermodel, trust me! I

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.260
know what it's like to be judged based
on my size!

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:50.050
But i'm also a mom and now one of my
life's greatest passions is to be a part

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:55.170
of creating a world where children can
grow up happy, successful and fulfilled

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:59.920
at any size. I hope you are willing to
join me in that effort. During this

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.420
program we're going to take a look at
what weight bias is, how it shows up at home

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:05.920
and school,

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:11.280
who its victims and sources are, what its
consequences are and what we as parents

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.779
and teachers can do

00:02:13.779 --> 00:02:15.069
to improve the lives of children

00:02:15.069 --> 00:02:16.219
we're surrounded by.

00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:19.620
But first, let's take a look at how prevalent

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.739
this problem is.

00:02:21.739 --> 00:02:27.619
Obesity in children and adults has
doubled in the past twenty years.

00:02:27.619 --> 00:02:32.129
Alarmingly, it's tripled in teens.

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:36.510
One in five American children is
overweight and overweight children

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.739
tend to become overweight adults.

00:02:38.739 --> 00:02:41.320
Thirty percent of adults are obese.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.930
And we're right on track for this trend to continue.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:48.329
There are many efforts underway to address 
childhood obesity,

00:02:48.329 --> 00:02:49.549
but we aren't going to solve the 

00:02:49.549 --> 00:02:52.049
nutritional and lifestyle changes that plague our 
nation in the 

00:02:52.049 --> 00:02:53.339
next twenty minutes,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.620
but,

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.419
what we are going to do

00:02:56.419 --> 00:02:59.159
is share with you some new perspectives
and tools that can help you

00:02:59.159 --> 00:03:01.580
as parents and teachers

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:02.640
stem the tide

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.540
of prejudice in our school system

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:09.419
and even at home so that children do not remain
vulnerable to the negative impact of 

00:03:09.419 --> 00:03:11.439
bias and stigma.

00:03:11.439 --> 00:03:11.749
And so that we may all

00:03:11.749 --> 00:03:18.749
begin to treat many overweight and obese people
already in our lives fairly.

00:03:24.279 --> 00:03:25.319
"Hey Ralph!"

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:31.469
"What's that? Your lunch box?"
/laughter/ "Ralph."

00:03:38.169 --> 00:03:44.589
"Hey Ralph." /laughter/

00:03:44.589 --> 00:03:48.549
Peers are frequent perpetrators of
weight bias, with school being the most

00:03:48.549 --> 00:03:50.079
common setting.

00:03:50.079 --> 00:03:53.959
Teasing can be in the form of verbal and
physical aggression as well as social

00:03:53.959 --> 00:03:55.409
exclusion.

00:03:55.409 --> 00:04:00.359
Many students face this torment daily. It
takes a toll on their emotional and

00:04:00.359 --> 00:04:01.519
physical health

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:04.229
and reduces their quality of life.

00:04:04.229 --> 00:04:09.539
One study even found that the quality of
life for obese children is as low as

00:04:09.539 --> 00:04:13.819
children with cancer.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.829
"My friend, um, was picked on 

00:04:16.829 --> 00:04:18.769
by a teacher,

00:04:18.769 --> 00:04:21.949
who, he called her,

00:04:21.949 --> 00:04:23.870
um, like, chubby and stuff,

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:27.509
and i just thought that was
very uncalled for, and a teacher

00:04:27.509 --> 00:04:30.789
shouldn't say anything like that.

00:04:30.789 --> 00:04:35.509
Twenty four percent of overweight boys
and thirty percent of overweight girls

00:04:35.509 --> 00:04:37.969
experience prejudice in middle school.

00:04:37.969 --> 00:04:43.039
That bias doubles in high school where
fifty-eight percent of adolescent boys

00:04:43.039 --> 00:04:48.699
and sixty-three percent of adolescent
girls are the victims of peer teasing.

00:04:48.699 --> 00:04:49.460
"Oh God,

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:51.830
here comes the earthquake."

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.760
I've heard my friends

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.619
talking about

00:04:55.619 --> 00:04:58.419
a girl who's only slightly heavier than me

00:04:58.419 --> 00:05:03.039
and, like, making fun of her, and it
makes me wonder what they said behind

00:05:03.039 --> 00:05:05.009
my back.

00:05:05.009 --> 00:05:09.310
Unfortunately attitudes towards weight 
among children worsen over time.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:13.470
We know that weight bias begins as
early as age three in preschool and 

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:17.650
continues throughout elementary school,
middle school, high school and even college.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:21.380
So overweight and obese children are vulnerable
targets of weight bias throughout their

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.039
educational careers.

00:05:23.039 --> 00:05:26.139
Studies showed that children as young as
three years old

00:05:26.139 --> 00:05:31.410
view overweight peers as mean, stupid,
ugly, unhappy, lazy,

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.289
having few friends,

00:05:33.289 --> 00:05:35.339
and undesirable as playmates.

00:05:35.339 --> 00:05:40.069
This all just based on the size of their
bodies by three years old!

00:05:40.069 --> 00:05:41.729
Where does this come from?

00:05:41.729 --> 00:05:45.180
Weight stigma comes from a series of
experiences that people have just

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:46.820
looking around them in their culture.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:52.470
They see how their parents discussed the
issue of weight, they see how their peers in schools discuss it,

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:57.150
they see overweight people ridiculed
on television shows and made fun of by

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:58.379
comics and the like, 

00:05:58.379 --> 00:06:02.219
and because of this, um... they
develop quite negative attitudes,

00:06:02.219 --> 00:06:04.360
they're very difficult to change.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:07.349
By the time the children are in high
school and college they're experiencing

00:06:07.349 --> 00:06:09.340
multiple forms of weight bias

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:13.030
not just verbal comments or physical
aggression, but also relational

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:16.299
victimization in the form of social
exclusion.

00:06:16.299 --> 00:06:17.840
A lot of people assume

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:21.129
that overweight people are dumb

00:06:21.129 --> 00:06:22.500
or lazy

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:28.560
but most of the time that's not the case.
In fact, I do well at school, I get good grades,

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:35.280
I'm part of the drama program, I
exercise, and I dance after school, so

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:36.400
it's not,

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.769
in most cases, it's not true.

00:06:39.769 --> 00:06:42.680
People are afraid of what's
different from them.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:47.349
And so by making them as less of
a person

00:06:47.349 --> 00:06:49.679
then i guess they feel empowered.

00:06:49.679 --> 00:06:51.440
Behind their back they might talk about,

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:55.220
'Oh, look at that shirt she was wearing. Her
stomach's popping out and everything. I can't

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:58.059
believe she'd even think of wearing
something like that.'

00:06:58.059 --> 00:06:59.840
They'll just say, like, all these, like

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:01.559
fat jokes about like

00:07:01.559 --> 00:07:05.689
wide load coming through and all
this stuff and it hurts me to see people

00:07:05.689 --> 00:07:09.189
getting treated, because I see how sad
they are.

00:07:09.189 --> 00:07:11.909
Most of the comments I get from them,
because some of them are my friends, they

00:07:11.909 --> 00:07:15.119
say they heard comments like that
before and you just get used to it.

00:07:15.119 --> 00:07:16.379
And that's a problem,

00:07:16.379 --> 00:07:17.620
that you're getting used to it,

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.479
that's something you're not supposed to
get used to.

00:07:20.479 --> 00:07:25.259
From nursery school through college
overweight students experience ostracism,

00:07:25.259 --> 00:07:25.930
discouragement,

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:30.449
and unfortunately even violence. For
overweight students, the school

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:34.930
experience is one of ongoing
prejudice, unnoticed discrimination and

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:37.039
almost constant harassment.

00:07:37.039 --> 00:07:40.349
Overweight children are more likely
than normal weight children to be

00:07:40.349 --> 00:07:41.799
victims of bullying.

00:07:41.799 --> 00:07:44.259
Obese children ages twelve to
sixteen

00:07:44.259 --> 00:07:47.689
are more often the victims of repeated
group aggression

00:07:47.689 --> 00:07:49.059
or mobbing.

00:07:49.059 --> 00:07:53.929
And sadly, as a defense mechanism, some of
them resort to becoming bullies

00:07:53.929 --> 00:07:55.169
themselves

00:07:55.169 --> 00:07:59.229
because they have nobody to turn to for
support or help.

00:07:59.229 --> 00:08:03.979
I've seen a couple kids that have been teased
turning into bullies because

00:08:03.979 --> 00:08:05.669
they

00:08:05.669 --> 00:08:10.219
basically are trying to get back at everybody that
has teased them and even people that

00:08:10.219 --> 00:08:11.960
haven't teased them and

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.729
and it's just they wanna

00:08:13.729 --> 00:08:16.819
put on his tough guy reputation

00:08:16.819 --> 00:08:20.129
and it just turns them into bully.

00:08:20.129 --> 00:08:24.310
The diet and beauty industries 
bombard us in and day out with the

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:27.659
myth of the achievable perfect body,

00:08:27.659 --> 00:08:31.789
perpetuating the cultural premium we
place on thinness.

00:08:31.789 --> 00:08:36.090
I think they might think that fat people
are nasty just because they don't have

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:40.010
the body of a super model or something,
'cause super models don't even have

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:45.980
that body. They re-touch by computer so why
does everyone think everyone has to look like that?

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:47.930
Clothes shopping is

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:50.040
one of my least favrote

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:54.580
times of year. Like, going back to school and
having to get a new wardrobe and

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:55.840
lots of times

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:58.360
the clothes don't fit.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:01.340
"I hate shopping!"

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:04.010
"Well, it might be fun if anything actually fit!"

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:05.630
"Let's just go home."

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:09.440
"You've got to find something,
you can't go naked!"

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.680
"Fashion's stupid!"

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:13.410
"Why can't I just wear something I
already have?"

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:14.770
"Because nothing you have fits."

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:17.670
It,

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:19.920
it makes me feel so, like

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:21.290
ugly.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:25.760
Weight stigma, blame and intolerance are
not constructive motivators for weight

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:29.780
loss. They can actually have the opposite
effect.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:33.930
Our research shows that social pressure
and stigma do not motivate weight loss,

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:36.120
and in fact, have the opposite effect.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:39.490
For example we surveyed over twenty four
hundred adults who were overweight and

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:43.810
obese and asked them about their experiences
of stigma and we found that people

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:49.110
reported coping with stigma by eating
more food and refusing to diet.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:49.660
My parents

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:51.720
try to be supported

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:55.130
but most of it just makes me feel worse.

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.630
They

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:59.570
say things to try and get me to
lose weight

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:01.430
but it doesn't help at all.

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:04.890
It kinda makes me want to eat more.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:09.360
Victims of weight bias are more
susceptible to loneliness, depression,

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.090
anxiety, low self-esteem

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:15.960
poor body image and suicidal thoughts
and behaviors. Look at this list! Is

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:19.020
this what we want for our children?
Certainly not.

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:21.760
But this is what weight stigma gives
them.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:26.440
A quality of life that no parent would
wish for their child.

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:30.290
We also know from research that children
who experience weight bias are more

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:33.740
likely to engage in unhealthy eating
behaviors, like binge eating,

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:37.410
and are more likely to avoid physical
activity, both of which may only

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:41.100
reinforce additional weight gain and obesity.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:45.530
Ramifications of stigma on quality of life
continue into adulthood.

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:48.369
One study that I found particularly
alarming

00:10:48.369 --> 00:10:53.859
was that women who were overweight as
children or teenagers still suffered

00:10:53.859 --> 00:10:59.170
significant wage penalties even after
they lost the excess weight.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:03.700
Weight bias is very socially acceptable in
North American society, it's rarely

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:05.440
challenged and often ignored,

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:09.340
and as a result, overweight and obesity
individuals have very little support when

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:13.680
they confront weight bias and as a result
may internalize negative stereotypes

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:17.660
and blame themselves for the negative
attitude that they see.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:23.199
The stereotypes that characterized
overweight and obese people as dumb,

00:11:23.199 --> 00:11:28.120
unsuccessful, stupid, or lazy, simply
aren't true! Think about the

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:32.670
overweight people already in your life!
Family members, friends, co-workers

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:33.730
children

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:37.070
Maybe even you've had a struggle with
your weight in the past.

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:42.410
We know that many people who are
overweight are intelligent, successful,

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:44.470
friendly and capable of achieving

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:48.030
the same goals as someone who is not
overweight.

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:50.910
People who are obese are just like
everybody else.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:55.190
they live, they breathe, they think, they're just
like everyone else. Just 'cause they're a 

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:59.530
little heavier than other people doesn't
mean that they're less of a person.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:02.860
Maybe they may have a couple extra
pounds, but that's it.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:06.090
Underneath it all, they're all just like us.

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:09.490
Expressing negative attitudes
towards obese people has become one of

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:12.640
the last accepted forms of prejudice

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:19.640
and could be as hurtful and difficult to
counter as racial prejudice.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:22.060
Um, I see teachers, like, say something

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:26.180
in passing and they don't even realize
that it's offensive

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.220
and

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:30.650
the teachers are any better than the
students sometimes.

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:33.400
I found a lot of the teachers weren't as

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.040
sympathetic as i thought,

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:38.050
that you would imagine a teacher should
be,

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:39.990
and support really wasn't there

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:42.100
for some of his

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:43.930
his years

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:46.730
and it really hurt him, it hurt him a lot.

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:51.170
You just feel low, and you
just don't know what to do,

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:52.510
so you

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:54.050
make, you try to, 

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:57.180
you try to comfort yourself with food

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:58.410
uh...

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:03.050
games inside all day or stuff like that.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:05.790
Overweight youth are not only teased at
school

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:10.840
but peer harassment can come in the form
of verbal teasing, physical bullying or

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:15.440
social rejection from family members too.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.540
"You're a disgusting, fat pig!"

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:19.200
"Well, she is turning into a little porker."

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:26.200
"Nothing you have fits."

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:31.080
What if your child is the victim of
weight bias?

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:34.530
Here are some suggestions of ways to
talk to your child about these issues

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:41.530
and find ways to intervene, offer support,
and help your child cope.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.410
"Hey there."
"Hi."

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:53.000
"How was your day?"
"It was alright."

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:56.850
"Just alright? Yeah?"

00:13:56.850 --> 00:14:01.100
I think one of the most important things
that needs to happen between a parent and

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:03.350
a child is open communication.

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:09.050
And that's really the groundwork that needs
to be set from the beginning. So you

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:11.800
want to have a relationship with your
child where they feel like they can come and

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:13.790
talk to you about a range of things.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:17.850
So things are going well in their lives
and things that aren't going so well. And 

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:22.810
one way to facilitate that is for the
parent to try to retain somewhat of a

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:28.570
neutral stance when their child starts
telling them about a difficult situation.

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:34.020
"These boys, uhÉ they called me fat."

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:36.660
"I don't really know who they are."

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:39.050
"Oh, sweetie, I'm sorry. I'm sorry that happened."

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:40.999
"When did that happen to you?"

00:14:40.999 --> 00:14:43.260
"At lunch."

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:48.250
If your child has had their
self-esteem damaged through a

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:51.440
situation where someone has
discriminated against because of their weight

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.449
or bullied them because of their weight.

00:14:53.449 --> 00:14:57.260
I think parents need to be very direct
and tell them

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:58.330
that

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:01.970
A) that they did not deserve to be
treated this way

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:05.950
and also to remind them of all the
strengths they have as a person.

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:08.410
"So how did that make you feel?"

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:10.530
"It really hurt."

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:15.260
"I feel like no one was there for me
or had my back."

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:17.450
"You know I have you back

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:19.790
always, right?"

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:22.250
and uh... you know

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:25.770
Mrs. Johnson, your English teacher?

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:30.440
I think she's somebody you could go to
and turn to. She loves you, you know that."

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:34.860
"She said, she said such lovely things about 
you at the open house."

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:38.990
"Okay, and I think that's someone you can
trust and turn to."

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:40.360
"Alright, sweetie?"
"Okay."

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:44.410
Well fortunately schools have
developed policies and procedures to

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:47.790
deal with bullying in recent years
they're much more aware of these

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:48.750
problems.

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:53.060
So it makes sense for the parent to work
with their child

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:57.640
on a plan to go to the school talk with
a guidance counselor, a principal, maybe a

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:01.210
trusted teacher and really think about
the best way that the child should

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:08.210
handle themselves in school to avoid
future situations.

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:12.490
So, what can we do? At home or in
the classroom?

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.459
As parents and teachers?

00:16:14.459 --> 00:16:15.960
There's a lot we can do.

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:17.279
The first step ti

00:16:17.279 --> 00:16:20.270
changing any stereotype or
eradicating prejudice

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:27.050
is to be aware. Start paying attention to
your own attitudes about weight. Educate

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:32.180
yourself about the causes of obesity so
that you will be informed. So that you

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:37.780
can help your children and students
understand the various causes of obesity.

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:43.290
The causes of obesity are very complex.
It is a combination of genetic factors,

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:43.950
environmental

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:49.279
factors, psychological factors and it's
important to recognize that so that

00:16:49.279 --> 00:16:53.570
when we look at someone and we see whatever
their body weight is, we don't make

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:55.279
assumptions about their behaviors

00:16:55.279 --> 00:16:57.710
based on that information.

00:16:57.710 --> 00:17:02.340
There's genetics involved, it's not just
like eating too much,

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:04.760
because I eat better than

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:08.580
a lot of people that I know and I
exercise more.

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:11.990
It's just the way I am.

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:13.070
Another thing people can do,

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:15.030
parents and teachers in particular,

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:17.170
to change the environment

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:20.089
of our children is what we call, avoid 'Fat-Talk'.

00:17:20.089 --> 00:17:21.430
And 'Fat-Talk' kinda goes like this,

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:25.760
it's when one person says "Oh, I feel so 
fat today."

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:30.100
And then the other person says, "Oh no, you're
not fat, I'm fat. Look at my thighs."

00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:33.970
And then the other person says, "Oh no, your thighs look great.
I'm the one who's really fat."

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:35.240
This is a problem

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:40.730
because when people talk this way, they are
communicating to children that

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:45.070
number one, your body size is a very important thing, and
number two, that how you feel on any

00:17:45.070 --> 00:17:46.740
given day is going to be related to 

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:50.000
whether or not you're feeling fat that day.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:54.600
Be alert to both overt and subtle forms of 
peer harassment that occur in the

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:59.720
classroom or on the playground. And intervene
when you see weight-based teasing.

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:05.770
Encourage your students to intervene and
stand for their peers.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:09.020
"Wouldn't it be quicker if you just smeared that on
your thighs?" /laughter/

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:11.789
"Yeah, can you say 'carbs'?"

00:18:11.789 --> 00:18:13.039
"What's your problem?"

00:18:13.039 --> 00:18:15.360
"What are you, the pig's keeper?" /laughter/

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:16.990
"Just leave her alone, okay?"

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:21.820
"Fine, whatever." 
My brother's saw people
making fun of me in school one day

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:24.160
and he came and he stood up for me,

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:31.160
and it makes me feel good to know that
somebody accepts me for who I am.

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:35.980
One problem right now is that it's very
rare for children to see role models

00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:40.299
who are not very thin or do not have an
ideal body type.

00:18:40.299 --> 00:18:43.249
So one thing parents and
teachers can do is they can really seek

00:18:43.249 --> 00:18:44.860
out this sort of individuals

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:49.020
and hold them up as role models for
children so they can look in the media,

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:51.419
they can look into sports,

00:18:51.419 --> 00:18:56.899
or other celebrities and find
people who can serve as role models and

00:18:56.899 --> 00:19:00.300
really represent very diverse body types.

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:05.770
Be sensitive to situations of potential
embarrassment for overweight students.

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:10.020
I actually spoke with a parent once who
told me about her daughter who was in

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:11.280
kindergarten

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:15.200
that when she arrived for school the
teacher had set up this special table

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:16.060
and chair

00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:19.800
in a completely separate area of the
classroom off away from the other

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:23.960
children because the teacher felt that
the child would not fit into the regular

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:24.540
desks

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:27.250
This is really an example of how

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:31.930
it is communicated to the child: you don't
fit in here and you don't belong here.

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:35.840
Treat weight tolerance with the same
significance as you would racial or

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:40.130
religious tolerance.

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:42.770
Try to promote awareness of weight
bias.

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:48.080
Be a role model by enforcing a zero
tolerance policy of weight-based teasing in

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.900
your classroom.

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:57.900
"Oh God, here comes the earthquake!"
"Hey! You go, Ralph! Come on Ralph!"
/cheering/

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:16.420
At the Rudd Center, we work hard to
eliminate the problem of weight bias.

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:20.760
We believe that there's a strong
social injustice occurring here.

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:24.180
The hundreds of millions of people
around the world are deeply affected by

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:28.990
this and it just doesn't need to occur.
Race bias doesn't need to occur.

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:33.720
Gender bias doesn't need to occur and
weight bias doesn't need to occur.

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:38.169
We all want the same things for our kids,
don't we?

00:20:38.169 --> 00:20:40.200
Happy, healthy childhoods.

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:44.340
Thank you so much for joining us today
and in the future as we strive to

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:48.990
improve the quality of life for our kids
through not just physical activity and

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:50.210
nutritious eating,

00:20:50.210 --> 00:20:54.700
but by creating a world where we can
all can be successful and fulfilled

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:57.530
at any weight.

00:20:57.530 --> 00:21:01.010
For more information please visit the
Rudd Center for Food

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:03.289
Policy and Obesity at YaleRuddCenter.org.

